% Precedence, associativity, and the operator families.

### name: op.prec.mul-over-add
--- source
2 + 3 * 4
--- expect
num 14
===
### name: op.prec.concat-looser-than-add
--- source
"a" & 1 + 2
--- expect
text "a3"
===
### name: op.prec.concat-tighter-than-compare
--- source
"a" & "b" $== "ab"
--- expect
bool TRUE
===
### name: op.prec.not-looser-than-compare
--- note
NOT binds looser than comparison, unlike C-family `!`. NOT 1 == 2 is NOT (1 == 2).
--- source
NOT 1 == 2
--- expect
bool TRUE
===
### name: op.prec.not-tighter-than-and
--- source
NOT TRUE AND FALSE
--- expect
bool FALSE
===
### name: op.prec.assign-looser-than-compare
--- source
A = 1 == 1; A
--- expect
bool TRUE
===
### name: op.prec.comma-looser-than-assign
--- note
A=3,4 is (A=3), 4 — a two element list, with A set to 3 along the way.
--- source
A = 3, 4
--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"3", "2"=t"4"}
===
### name: op.prec.semicolon-looser-than-comma
--- source
(1, 2; 3, 4)
--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"3", "2"=t"4"}
===
### name: op.compare.no-chaining
--- source
1 < 2 < 3
--- expect
error E_SYNTAX at 1:7
===
### name: op.unary-minus
--- source
- 2 - -3
--- expect
num 1
===

### name: op.concat.text
--- source
"A" & "B"
--- expect
text "AB"
===
### name: op.concat.number-is-text
--- source
2 & "A"
--- expect
text "2A"
===
### name: op.concat.bin-wins
--- source
"A" & FROM_HEX("42")
--- expect
bin 4142
===
### name: op.concat.rejects-bool
--- source
"a" & TRUE
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:7
===
### name: op.arith.rejects-text
--- source
3 + "A"
--- expect
error E_NOT_NUM at 1:5
===

### name: op.text-compare.bytewise
--- source
"A" $< "B"
--- expect
bool TRUE
===
### name: op.text-compare.astral-is-byte-order
--- note
JS compares strings in UTF-16 order natively, which would make this FALSE.
The spec requires UTF-8 byte order, where U+1F44D sorts after U+FFFD.
--- source
"\u{FFFD}" $< "\u{1F44D}"
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: op.logic.and
--- source
TRUE AND FALSE
--- expect
bool FALSE
===
### name: op.logic.and-short-circuits
--- source
FALSE AND (1 / 0 == 0)
--- expect
bool FALSE
===
### name: op.logic.or-short-circuits
--- source
TRUE OR (1 / 0 == 0)
--- expect
bool TRUE
===
### name: op.logic.xor
--- source
TRUE XOR TRUE
--- expect
bool FALSE
===
### name: op.logic.no-truthiness
--- source
"x" AND TRUE
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:1
===
### name: op.logic.not
--- source
NOT FALSE
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: op.bitwise.and
--- source
FROM_HEX("f0") BAND FROM_HEX("31")
--- expect
bin 30
===
### name: op.bitwise.or
--- source
FROM_HEX("f0") BOR FROM_HEX("0f")
--- expect
bin ff
===
### name: op.bitwise.xor
--- source
FROM_HEX("ff") BXOR FROM_HEX("80")
--- expect
bin 7f
===
### name: op.bitwise.length-mismatch
--- source
FROM_HEX("00") BOR FROM_HEX("0102")
--- expect
error E_LEN_MISMATCH
===

### name: op.assign.returns-value
--- source
A = 2
--- expect
num 2
===
### name: op.assign.compound
--- source
A = 1; A += 2; A *= 3; A
--- expect
num 9
===
### name: op.assign.compound-concat
--- source
A = "x"; A &= "y"; A
--- expect
text "xy"
===
### name: op.assign.compound-needs-target
--- source
A += 1
--- expect
error E_UNDEF_VAR
===
### name: op.assign.copies-by-value
--- source
A = (1, 2); B = A; B[1] = 9; A[1]
--- expect
num 1
===
### name: op.assign.bad-target
--- source
3 = 4
--- expect
error E_BAD_ASSIGN at 1:1
===
### name: op.seq.yields-last
--- source
1; 2; 3
--- expect
num 3
===
### name: op.seq.trailing-semicolon
--- source
1; 2;
--- expect
num 2
===
